If I read those spoilers correctly...












You only get the 'lower' of your skills.  So in your case you get -3/+1 and
no +2 bonus.  However, if you happen to use weapon you are untrained, and
has -4/-2 skill bonus (say, you are double wielding sabers without actually
advancing in the sabers while being expert in 2-weapon), you actually
get -4/-2 on those weapons, since those modifiers are lower than the
two-weapon skill bonus.

Or, if you use dagger at expert in your primary hand, and saber at untrained
in your off hand and are expert at two weapon combat, you's get -3/+1 on
your dagger attacks (Since -3/+1 from being expert two weapon user is lower
bonus than +3/+2 Dagger Expert bonus), and you get -2 damage penalty on your
saber attacks (as far as I know, there's no 'to-hit' bonus involved for off
hand weapons).

So, "no cumlative bonuses, and always uses lower of the relevant skills" is
what I understand how two weapon combat works.

